                ("bionic_leg", 0.3), ("reinforced_spine", 0.2), ("synthetic_heart", 0.15)]),
    ],
    // What mining one cell of rock or ore yields (soil yields nothing).
    rock_drops: ("stone", 6),
    ore_drops: ("iron_ore", 4),
    copper_drops: ("copper_ore", 4),
    // Where things made from components are taken apart (salvage recipes are made from their recipes).
    salvage_bench: Some("salvage_bench"),

    // Player-built structures, listed in the toolbar menu named by
    // `category`. `special` marks behaviour the game handles in code: `Floor`
    // (a slab others stand on, built in the air), `Roof` (never in the menu:
    // put over enclosed rooms by themselves; the look is only its blueprint,
    // the roof itself is drawn in code), `Stairs` (connect a cell to
    // the one above), `Bed` (sleep and recover), `Door` (swings open),
    // `Table` and `Seat` (colonists eat sitting at a table), `Grave` (dug into
    // soil; a dead colonist is buried in it; parts with `filled` show only
    // while it is or isn't filled).
    // `beauty` counts towards the quality of the room it's in (or borders);
    // `daylight` lights the rooms it borders; `storage` holds `slots` stacks
    // (of up to 50 each, usually different things) per cell, shown at
    // `height` (and `lower` for slots 3 and 4). `along_walls`: modelled spanning x, turned to run along the walls
    // beside it (doors, windows). Parts with `link` only show when the
    // neighbour that way is the same structure or a wall. `look: Opening`
    // is a wall block with a hole (windows), drawn with the walls. `cost` is
    // one amount or a list, brought in that order. Removing a structure drops
    // `drops`, or half of each of its costs if not given. `power`: watts made
    // (`output`) and watt-hours stored (`storage`), shown only for now;
    // `open_sky`: can't be built under a roof. `look: Block`
    // means it is drawn as a solid block with the terrain (walls); its parts
    // only matter otherwise.
    // `cover` in battle: None, Light, Medium or Heavy (heavy blocks the view;
    // default: Heavy if it blocks sight, Medium if it can't be walked through,
    // else Light).
